---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Contact | Send Josh — Josh Montague, Training Leaders International"
  description="Contact Josh Montague about mission partnership, financial support, or hosting a Bible seminar at your church."
  path="/contact/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <h1>Start a conversation.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.15rem;">Whether your church is exploring partnership, your missions team has questions, or you'd like to host a seminar &mdash; Josh would love to hear from you.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule section-panel">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Reach Josh</p>
        <h2>Email is best.</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.05rem;"><a href="mailto:josh.montague@trainingleaders.org">josh.montague@trainingleaders.org</a></p>
        <p>Josh travels overseas several times a year, so allow a few days for a reply when he's in the field.</p>
        <p class="sidebar-head" style="margin-top:32px;">Elsewhere</p>
        <ul style="list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0; line-height:2;">
          <li><a href="https://trainingleadersinternational.org">Training Leaders International</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.crossgrace.org">Cross of Grace Church (Chaska, MN)</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="photo">
        <img src="/images/josh-headshot.jpg" alt="Josh Montague" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio:4/5; object-fit:cover;" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">For event hosts</p>
      <h2>A ready-to-read introduction.</h2>
      <p style="max-width:62ch;">Hosting Josh at your church or event? Here's an introduction you can read as written.</p>
      <blockquote style="max-width:68ch;">
        Our speaker today is Dr. Josh Montague. Josh pastored churches in Michigan and Wisconsin for fifteen years before joining Training Leaders International, where he now serves as Training Strategist &mdash; training pastors around the world who have no access to theological education. He has taught the Scriptures to pastors on five continents, from Serbia to Togo to the Philippines, and serves as a teaching elder at Cross of Grace Church in Chaska, Minnesota. He holds a Doctor of Intercultural Studies from Western Seminary, and he and his wife, Mary Ann, have four children. Please welcome Josh Montague.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
